    <string name="title_disclaimer">Before you continue</string>
    <string name="msg_disclaimer_body">This tool unpacks a Minecraft installation package, rewrites it and signs it again, then writes the result next to the original file. Please read the following before you continue.

1. Back up first
- Worlds, resource packs, shaders, add-ons, skins and settings: copy them somewhere else. A failed repack, the wrong version, or a package name clash can all leave the game unable to read what was there before.
- Worlds especially: a coexistence build shares the same world folder as the original, and uninstalling either one can take the worlds with it.

2. About signatures
- If the new package uses the **same signature** as the original, it installs straight over the top and your data is untouched. Nothing to worry about in that case.
- If the signature changes (MT default, zihao_il, or your own .bks), Android treats it as a different app. You **must uninstall the original first**, and uninstalling deletes the app data.
- So: back up before changing the signature, or use **Coexistence processing** instead — it renames the package so both builds can live side by side.

3. Coexistence mode
- It only changes the package name, not the world path, so both builds share one world folder.
- Running both at the same time and writing to the same world can overwrite each other. Keep one open at a time.

4. Everything else
- This is an unofficial tool. It has no affiliation with Mojang or Microsoft. You accept the risk of corrupted worlds, lost data, account issues or device problems caused by using it.
- After a game update the patch may stop working until a matching signature ships.
- Do not redistribute the patched package as an official build, and do not sell it.

Tapping **OK** means you have read and understood the above.</string>
